  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 500eb (Expensive)</p>\n<p><em>“FUCK ARMOR PENALTIES.” — Anonymous Lizard</em></p>\n<p><strong>SP 16 or lower Body/Head Armor Enhancement. Cannot be installed in any form of Metalgear.</strong> All of the armor’s Armor Penalties (if any), are reduced by 1 (Minimum 0). Armor with this enhancement cannot be combined with a kit or tech upgraded to resemble any form of Fashion it does not already appear as by default. This enhancement cannot be Tech Upgraded to further reduce Armor Penalties.</p>\n<p><strong>Type:</strong> Armor Enhancement (Body/Head, SP 16 or lower, not Metalgear)<br>\n<strong>Attachment slots:</strong> 0</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Armor Enhancement rules: one Enhancement per piece of armor (armor worn on both body and head counts as one piece); not for cyberware armor (Skinweave, Subdermal Armor) or armor that's part of an ACPA or vehicle; SP limits use the armor's fully repaired SP; a Tech installs or removes one in 1 hour with no check; they don't count as Tech Upgrades for Upgrade Expertise. Armor Attachments have no limit per armor unless stated.</li>\n<li>All of the armor's Armor Penalties drop by 1 (minimum 0); lower its penalty by hand.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Armor &amp; Fashion &gt; Armor Enhancements &amp; Kits).</em></p>"
